    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "For each k, each group of order k is totally k-closed, while the alternating group\nAk is not totally (k − 2)-closed. Is there a fixed integer k such that all finite simple\ngroups which are not alternating groups are totally k-closed?\n                          M. Arezoomand, M. A. Iranmanesh, C. E. Praeger, G. Tracey",
